"# aos-lock: a lock next to a file or folder\n\n```sh\naos-lock acquire --note editing f.txt     # creates f.txt.lock/ (for a folder d: d/.lock/); prints nothing\naos-lock show f.txt                       # {\"holder\": \"/work\", \"acquired_at\": \"...\", \"note\": \"editing\"}\naos-lock release f.txt\n```\n\nExit 10 = the lock is taken (acquire), held by someone else (release: nothing released, one warning), or not there (show). `--wait-ms N` waits up to N ms; `--lease-cycles N` lets the lease expire after N clock cycles. The holder is your `AOS_WS`, `AOS_STACK`, `AOS_CF` or the current folder. `release --force` releases someone else's lock. Releasing a lock that is not there = `LockMissing`. Half-removed lock folders are cleaned by the sweeper.\n"
